+# KWin Screencast DBus API
+
+## Overview
+
+KWin exposes active screencast streams via DBus using the ObjectManager pattern. This allows third-party applications to monitor which screens, windows, or regions are being recorded, and by which application.
+
+## Use Cases
+
+- **Recording indicators**: Show visual indicators when screen recording is active
+- **Privacy tools**: Alert users when sensitive windows are being captured
+- **System monitoring**: Track which applications are consuming screen capture resources
+- **Integration**: Build custom UI for managing active recordings
+
+## DBus Service Details
+
+| Property | Value |
+|----------|-------|
+| **Bus** | Session bus |
+| **Service** | `org.kde.KWin` |
+| **Root Path** | `/org/kde/KWin/ScreenCast` |
+| **Root Interface** | `org.freedesktop.DBus.ObjectManager` |
+
+## Stream Objects
+
+Each active screencast stream is exposed as a DBus object with the path:
+
+```
+/org/kde/KWin/ScreenCast/node_<pipewire_node_id>
+```
+
+For example: `/org/kde/KWin/ScreenCast/node_42`
+
+## Interfaces
+
+### Common Interface: `org.kde.KWin.ScreenCast`
+
+Present on all stream objects, regardless of type.
+
+| Property | Type | Description |
+|----------|------|-------------|
+| `Identifier` | `s` (string) | PipeWire node ID as string |
+| `Type` | `s` (string) | Stream type: `"window"`, `"output"`, or `"region"` |
+| `State` | `i` (int) | Stream state (0=idle, 1=paused, 2=streaming) |
+| `ConsumerApp` | `s` (string) | Name of consuming application (e.g., `"obs"`, `"firefox"`) |
+| `ConsumerPID` | `u` (uint32) | Process ID of consumer application (0 if unknown) |
+
+**Note:** `ConsumerApp` and `ConsumerPID` may initially be empty when a stream is created. Listen for the `PropertiesChanged` signal to get updates when the consumer connects.
+
+### Window Stream: `org.kde.KWin.ScreenCast.Window`
+
+Additional interface for window screencasts (when `Type` is `"window"`).
+
+| Property | Type | Description |
+|----------|------|-------------|
+| `WindowId` | `s` (string) | Window UUID |
+| `WindowClass` | `s` (string) | X11 resource class |
+| `ResourceName` | `s` (string) | X11 resource name |
+| `Caption` | `s` (string) | Window title |
+| `X` | `d` (double) | Window X position |
+| `Y` | `d` (double) | Window Y position |
+| `Width` | `i` (int) | Window width in pixels |
+| `Height` | `i` (int) | Window height in pixels |
+
+**Note:** Window geometry (`X`, `Y`, `Width`, `Height`) may initially be `0` or invalid. Wait for `PropertiesChanged` signal before relying on geometry values.
+
+### Output Stream: `org.kde.KWin.ScreenCast.Output`
+
+Additional interface for full-screen/monitor screencasts (when `Type` is `"output"`).
+
+| Property | Type | Description |
+|----------|------|-------------|
+| `OutputName` | `s` (string) | Name of the output (e.g., `"HDMI-1"`) |
+| `X` | `d` (double) | Output X position |
+| `Y` | `d` (double) | Output Y position |
+| `Width` | `i` (int) | Output width in pixels |
+| `Height` | `i` (int) | Output height in pixels |
+
+### Region Stream: `org.kde.KWin.ScreenCast.Region`
+
+Additional interface for region screencasts (when `Type` is `"region"`).
+
+| Property | Type | Description |
+|----------|------|-------------|
+| `X` | `d` (double) | Region X position |
+| `Y` | `d` (double) | Region Y position |
+| `Width` | `i` (int) | Region width in pixels |
+| `Height` | `i` (int) | Region height in pixels |
+| `Scale` | `d` (double) | Scale factor |
+
+## Signals
+
+### `InterfacesAdded`
+
+Emitted when a new screencast stream is created.
+
+**Signature:** `oa{sa{sv}}`
+- `objectPath` (QDBusObjectPath): Path to the new stream object
+- `interfacesAndProperties` (QVariantMap): Map of interface names to their properties
+
+### `InterfacesRemoved`
+
+Emitted when a screencast stream ends.
+
+**Signature:** `oas`
+- `objectPath` (QDBusObjectPath): Path to the removed stream object
+- `interfaces` (QStringList): List of interface names that were removed
+
+### `PropertiesChanged`
+
+Standard DBus property change notification (per-object signal on `org.freedesktop.DBus.Properties`).
+
+**Important Properties to Monitor:**
+- `ConsumerApp` / `ConsumerPID`: Emitted when consumer connects (asynchronous)
+- Window geometry (`X`, `Y`, `Width`, `Height`): Emitted when window is moved/resized
+
+## Example Code
+
+### Python (PyQt6)
+
+```python
+from PyQt6.QtCore import QCoreApplication
+from PyQt6.QtDBus import QDBusConnection, QDBusInterface, QDBusReply
+
+def list_active_screencasts():
+    """List all active screencast streams."""
+    bus = QDBusConnection.sessionBus()
+    iface = QDBusInterface(
+        "org.kde.KWin",
+        "/org/kde/KWin/ScreenCast",
+        "org.freedesktop.DBus.ObjectManager",
+        bus
+    )
+
+    reply = iface.call("GetManagedObjects")
+    if reply.type() == QDBusReply.Error:
+        print(f"Error: {reply.error().message()}")
+        return
+
+    objects = reply.arguments()[0]
+
+    for path, interfaces in objects.items():
+        print(f"\nStream: {path}")
+
+        # Common properties
+        common = interfaces.get("org.kde.KWin.ScreenCast", {})
+        print(f"  Type: {common.get('Type')}")
+        print(f"  Consumer: {common.get('ConsumerApp')} (PID: {common.get('ConsumerPID')})")
+        print(f"  State: {common.get('State')}")
+
+        # Type-specific properties
+        stream_type = common.get('Type')
+        if stream_type == 'window':
+            window = interfaces.get("org.kde.KWin.ScreenCast.Window", {})
+            print(f"  Window: {window.get('Caption')}")
+            print(f"  Geometry: {window.get('X')}, {window.get('Y')} - {window.get('Width')}x{window.get('Height')}")
+        elif stream_type == 'output':
+            output = interfaces.get("org.kde.KWin.ScreenCast.Output", {})
+            print(f"  Output: {output.get('OutputName')}")
+        elif stream_type == 'region':
+            region = interfaces.get("org.kde.KWin.ScreenCast.Region", {})
+            print(f"  Region: {region.get('X')}, {region.get('Y')} - {region.get('Width')}x{region.get('Height')}")
+
+if __name__ == "__main__":
+    app = QCoreApplication([])
+    list_active_screencasts()
+```
+
+### Python (GDBus)
+
+```python
+from gi.repository import GLib, Gio
+
+def on_interfaces_added(connection, sender, path, interface, signal, params, user_data):
+    """Called when a new screencast stream is created."""
+    object_path, interfaces_and_properties = params
+
+    print(f"New screencast stream: {object_path}")
+
+    # Get common properties
+    common = interfaces_and_properties.get('org.kde.KWin.ScreenCast', {})
+    print(f"  Type: {common.get('Type')}")
+    print(f"  Consumer: {common.get('ConsumerApp')}")
+
+def on_interfaces_removed(connection, sender, path, interface, signal, params, user_data):
+    """Called when a screencast stream ends."""
+    object_path, interfaces = params
+    print(f"Screencast ended: {object_path}")
+
+def monitor_screencasts():
+    """Monitor screencast streams in real-time."""
+    bus = Gio.bus_get_sync(Gio.BusType.SESSION, None)
+
+    # Subscribe to InterfacesAdded
+    bus.signal_subscribe(
+        'org.kde.KWin',
+        'org.freedesktop.DBus.ObjectManager',
+        'InterfacesAdded',
+        '/org/kde/KWin/ScreenCast',
+        None,
+        Gio.DBusSignalFlags.NONE,
+        on_interfaces_added,
+        None
+    )
+
+    # Subscribe to InterfacesRemoved
+    bus.signal_subscribe(
+        'org.kde.KWin',
+        'org.freedesktop.DBus.ObjectManager',
+        'InterfacesRemoved',
+        '/org/kde/KWin/ScreenCast',
+        None,
+        Gio.DBusSignalFlags.NONE,
+        on_interfaces_removed,
+        None
+    )
+
+    print("Monitoring screencasts. Press Ctrl+C to exit.")
+
+    # Run event loop
+    loop = GLib.MainLoop()
+    try:
+        loop.run()
+    except KeyboardInterrupt:
+        pass
+
+if __name__ == "__main__":
+    monitor_screencasts()
+```
+
+### C++ (Qt)
+
+```cpp
+#include <QCoreApplication>
+#include <QDBusConnection>
+#include <QDBusInterface>
+#include <QDBusReply>
+#include <QDebug>
+
+void listActiveScreencasts()
+{
+    QDBusInterface iface(
+        QStringLiteral("org.kde.KWin"),
+        QStringLiteral("/org/kde/KWin/ScreenCast"),
+        QStringLiteral("org.freedesktop.DBus.ObjectManager"),
+        QDBusConnection::sessionBus()
+    );
+
+    QDBusReply<QVariantMap> reply = iface.call(QStringLiteral("GetManagedObjects"));
+    if (!reply.isValid()) {
+        qWarning() << "Error:" << reply.error().message();
+        return;
+    }
+
+    QVariantMap objects = reply.value();
+
+    for (auto it = objects.constBegin(); it != objects.constEnd(); ++it) {
+        const QString path = it.key();
+        const QVariantMap interfaces = it.value().toMap();
+
+        qDebug() << "Stream:" << path;
+
+        // Common properties
+        QVariantMap common = interfaces.value(QStringLiteral("org.kde.KWin.ScreenCast")).toMap();
+        qDebug() << "  Type:" << common.value(QStringLiteral("Type")).toString();
+        qDebug() << "  Consumer:" << common.value(QStringLiteral("ConsumerApp")).toString();
+        qDebug() << "  State:" << common.value(QStringLiteral("State")).toInt();
+
+        // Type-specific properties
+        QString type = common.value(QStringLiteral("Type")).toString();
+        if (type == QLatin1String("window")) {
+            QVariantMap window = interfaces.value(QStringLiteral("org.kde.KWin.ScreenCast.Window")).toMap();
+            qDebug() << "  Window:" << window.value(QStringLiteral("Caption")).toString();
+        } else if (type == QLatin1String("output")) {
+            QVariantMap output = interfaces.value(QStringLiteral("org.kde.KWin.ScreenCast.Output")).toMap();
+            qDebug() << "  Output:" << output.value(QStringLiteral("OutputName")).toString();
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+int main(int argc, char *argv[])
+{
+    QCoreApplication app(argc, argv);
+    listActiveScreencasts();
+    return 0;
+}
+```
+
+### Bash (qdbus)
+
+```bash
+#!/bin/bash
+
+# List all active screencasts
+qdbus org.kde.KWin /org/kde/KWin/ScreenCast org.freedesktop.DBus.ObjectManager.GetManagedObjects | grep -E "node_|Type|ConsumerApp"
+
+# Monitor for new screencasts
+dbus-monitor --session "type='signal',sender='org.kde.KWin',path='/org/kde/KWin/ScreenCast',interface='org.freedesktop.DBus.ObjectManager',member='InterfacesAdded'"
+```
+
+## Security Considerations
+
+### Privacy
+
+The screencast DBus interface exposes:
+- Window titles and positions
+- Which applications are being recorded
+- PID of recording applications
+
+This information is **read-only** and limited to the **session bus** (same user), but could be considered sensitive in multi-user scenarios.
+
+### Authorization
+
+- Screencast streams are created via **xdg-desktop-portal**, which handles user authorization
+- The DBus interface only exposes **already-authorized** streams
+- No additional authorization is required to read stream metadata
+- All introspection attempts are logged for audit purposes
+
+### Best Practices
+
+1. **Don't rely on immediate data**: Consumer info is populated asynchronously
+2. **Handle missing geometry**: Window geometry may be invalid initially
+3. **Subscribe to signals**: Use `PropertiesChanged` for real-time updates
+4. **Handle disconnections**: KWin restart will remove all stream objects
+5. **Validate data**: Check for null/empty values before using properties
+
+## Troubleshooting
+
+### No streams visible
+
+- Ensure KWin is running with Wayland backend
+- Check that a screencast is actually active (e.g., via OBS, Firefox screen sharing)
+- Verify DBus connection: `qdbus org.kde.KWin /org/kde/KWin/ScreenCast`
+
+### Empty ConsumerApp/ConsumerPID
+
+This is **normal** - consumer detection is asynchronous and takes 10-500ms:
+- Subscribe to `PropertiesChanged` signal
+- Poll periodically (not recommended)
+- Accept that some streams may never identify their consumer
+
+### Window geometry is 0x0
+
+This is **normal** for newly created window streams:
+- Subscribe to `PropertiesChanged` on `org.kde.KWin.ScreenCast.Window`
+- Wait for first geometry update (usually < 100ms)
+- Consider using window `WindowId` to track the window independently
+
+### Stream disappears immediately
+
+Streams are removed when:
+- User stops screen sharing
+- Recording application disconnects
+- KWin restarts
+- Window is closed (for window streams)
+
+## API Stability
+
+This API is **stable** and follows KDE's compatibility guarantees:
+- Property names and types will not change
+- New properties may be added in future versions
+- Signals will maintain backward compatibility
+- Interface names are stable
+
+## Version History
+
+- **KWin 6.6** (2025): Initial DBus interface implementation
